Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:45:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key and the release signature

Refresh gpgkey-B818B9CADF9089C2D5CEC66B75AD65802A0B4211.asc from
keyservers: same certificate(s), with self-signatures our copy was
missing.
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.
Replace libtpms-0.10.2.tar.gz.asc with the release signature upstream
made again with the updated key (SHA512, 2026-11-10), from
https://github.com/stefanberger/libtpms/releases/download/v0.10.2/v0.10.2.tar.gz.asc.
libtpms-0.10.2.tar.gz.asc was in the lookaside cache, which a pull
request cannot update, so it moves into git (dropped from sources).

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
